  "description": "QADYUT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C38 H90 O8 Yb8. From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors; Yb6 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors; Yb7 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors; Yb8 (Yb) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.226-4.706 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 83.04-167.35°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C38H90O8Yb8.",
